  Static review only; no tests were run. I could not append the report because this role remains read-only. The following is ready to append to the findings file.

  ## Round 3 confirmation

  ### 1. Universal fail-fast — accept

  `publish-guest!` checks every result for `:status :refused` and throws `ex-info` with the complete result as `ex-data` (`test/yang/call/conformance.clj:50-58`). All four kit guest-publication sites use it:

  - `published-php`: `conformance.clj:61-66`
  - `published-py`: `conformance.clj:69-74`
  - `published-clj`: `conformance.clj:77-82`
  - `publish-donor!`: `conformance.clj:207-233`

  A search of `test/yang/call` finds no remaining direct `h/publish-guest-module!` or `publish-module!` call outside the guarded helper. Address extraction now occurs only after successful publication. Finding 4 is resolved.

  ### 2. Per-row error routing — accept

  `error-results` preserves the original Throwable under every backend (`test/yang/call/conformance.clj:462-465`). The wrappers cover both donor/runtime dereferences and composition construction:

  - `run-exception-program`: `conformance.clj:468-492`
  - `run-leg` and `run-pair`: `test/yang/call/exception_legs.clj:211-222,242-271`
  - `run-fixture` and `run-frontend`: `test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:161-203`

  `run-pair` and `run-frontend` replicate caught operational exceptions across their existing row IDs, so the tests receive per-backend Throwables and report `ex-data` through `:host/data`. Exceptions are preserved rather than relabelled as guest outcomes.

  Non-refusal exceptions also remain operational errors with their original object and data; they are not silently swallowed. Normal red/green values do not enter these catches. The existing `some Throwable` fallback still isolates each fixture through an independent `run-fixture` call, and each isolated call handles its own failure, so one poisoned fixture cannot erase the others (`exception_probes.clj:193-199`).

  ### 3. Green/red behavior — accept

  The successful paths are structurally unchanged: publication returns its original result, `run-exception-program` returns the same backend map, and pair/provenance batching and fallback conditions are unchanged. The new catches affect only exceptions that previously escaped before row reporting.

  The orchestrator’s focused results—9 F / 0 E, 6 F / 18 E, and 18 F / 21 E—match the ledger totals. This review did not independently rerun them.

  ### 4. Verification note — accept

  The round-3 correction also fixes the round-2 PHP row-name prose using the canonical ledger identifiers. No remaining contradiction was found between the corrected accounting and the ledger.

  ACCEPT

